{
  "id": "Compound::DB00674 - Gene::1136",
  "verbalization": "Galantamine is implicated in the regulation of acetylcholine-activated cation-selective channel activity through its interaction with multiple targets, including Chrng, Chrna9, and Chrne. These targets participate in the same biological process, which is the activation of cation-selective channels in response to acetylcholine. The evidence suggests that Galantamine may influence the function of these channels by binding to their respective targets, thereby modulating the activity of the channels and ultimately affecting the cellular response to acetylcholine. The shared involvement of these targets in the same pathway implies a potential mechanism by which Galantamine exerts its pharmacological effects, likely through the modulation of ion channel activity. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of ion channels in neurotransmission and suggests that Galantamine may act as a modulator of these channels, contributing to its therapeutic effects.",
